I'm using fvwm, and with my current fvwm configuration, bluetooth-applet is 
unusable.  I couldn't get it to be useful with windowmaker either (with what I 
think is the default debian config).  I eventually discovered that it works 
with fluxbox (also in a default-ish config).

Is there any good documentation about what features bluez-gnome requires from 
a window manager?  I guess it's something like a dock/wharf/tray feature, but 
I can't find any confirmation of that.

For FVWM, it's probably just a matter of activating the right "module".

Also, (as a sort of feature-request) is anyone working on getting bluez-gnome 
to work everywhere (e.g. with twm)?  Maybe some sort of fall-back 
functionality where it can just create a icon or a small window, when the 
dock/wharf/tray it prefers is not available?




